  "description": "In this video, Tika Kumari Budha, a childhood development trainer from Jungkot, Rolpa district, Nepal, speaks in the Sheshi Kham variety of the Kham Magar language. Interviewed by Uday Raj Aaley and recorded by Deewash Thapa in Jungkot on 17 July 2026 for OpenSpeaks Archives. She talks about her family's farming year, with corn sown in the Jeth (Jyeshtha) and Baisakh months, barley and wheat in November and December, and mustard and millet. Women wove aloe fibre into thread and mats while men sowed and ploughed, and in winter many men went to Butwal, Bhairawa, Kathmandu and India or other countries abroad to earn money. Sheshi Kham and Nepali subtitles are by Budha, transcribed and typed by Aaley, and English translations are by Panigrahi. Video edited by Panigrahi.",
